{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Between Me and between the children of Israel it is a sign forever.</b> It is possible to interpret that the word לעולם is explained thus: the Sabbath is a sign and token for the renewal of the world, and therefore He added to explain how it is a sign for the renewal of the world: 'for in six days YHWH made the heaven and the earth.' And the expression 'between Me and between the children of Israel' indicates a matter that is hidden, delivered in secrecy, and it alludes to the hidden matter that is in the commandment of the Sabbath. For a king who charges his son or his faithful servant: 'remember the matters that are between Me and you' — these are hidden, said only from mouth to mouth and not given to be written down. From this the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in tractate Yom Tov: Rabbi Shimon ben Yochai said, all the commandments that the Holy One, blessed be He, gave to Israel He gave them in public, except for the Sabbath, which He gave them in secrecy, as it is said: 'between Me and between the children of Israel it is a sign forever.' And how was the commandment of the Sabbath given in secrecy, when it was given in public — for it is included among the Ten Commandments that all the nations heard? And likewise Scripture says (Isaiah 48:16): ״לא מראש בסתר דברתי״, and likewise David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 138:4): ״יודוך ה׳ כל מלכי ארץ כי שמעו אמרי פיך״. Rather, the Sages intended the hidden matter that is in the commandment of the Sabbath, for that is what was given in secrecy, and therefore He used the expression 'between Me and between you.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:05.458089706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}